.TH SHOAL 1 "July 2026" "Shoal 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
shoal \- run the Shoal language and interactive shell
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B shoal
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ script
.IR args ...]
.br
.B shoal
.I command
.RI [ args ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Shoal evaluates structured, typed shell programs either in an interactive editor,
from standard input, from a source file, or from an inline command.
Interactive mode normally communicates with an isolated private execution kernel;
.B \-\-standalone
runs the evaluator in-process without the kernel protocol.
Scripts, inline commands, and standard-input programs are already local,
non-interactive evaluator runs; for those modes the option is an explicit,
idempotent selection.
Script arguments are exposed to source as the
.B args
list, and the source path is exposed as
.BR script .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c , " \-\-command " SOURCE
Evaluate SOURCE instead of reading a file or standard input.
Remaining arguments populate the Shoal
.B args
list.
.TP
.B \-\-standalone
Use local evaluation. This skips the private kernel in interactive mode;
non-interactive execution is already local. It does not select a separate language.
.TP
.BR \-h , " \-\-help"
Print complete command help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V , " \-\-version"
Print the version and exit.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B kernel
Start, inspect, or stop the resident kernel with
.BR start ,
.BR status ,
or
.BR stop .
Pass
.B \-\-json
after the action for a structured response.
An explicit start records an owner-only supervisor credential for the matching stop;
.B SHOAL_TOKEN
overrides that managed credential when set.
.TP
.B fmt
Format Shoal source or use
.B \-\-check
to report whether files would change without writing them.
.TP
.B doctor
Diagnose paths, configuration, platform support, sandboxing, and companions;
.B \-\-json
emits the full structured report.
.TP
.B lsp
Launch the
.BR shoal-lsp (1)
companion.
.TP
.B mcp
Launch the
.BR shoal-mcp (1)
companion.
.TP
.B completions
Generate bash, zsh, or fish completion source.
.TP
.B prompt
Print, explain, or benchmark a configured prompt side.
.B \-\-side SIDE
selects left, right, continuation, or transient;
.B \-\-n N
sets the benchmark sample count.
.SH OUTPUT
Command text and structured values are rendered on standard output.
Warnings and source-located parse or evaluation diagnostics are written to standard error.
.SH ERRORS
Unreadable, non-regular, oversized, or non-UTF-8 source is rejected before evaluation.
Parse errors return status 2; evaluation errors retain a valid typed status where possible.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
shoal
shoal --standalone -c 'math.sqrt(9)'
shoal scripts/check.shl release
shoal doctor --json
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success and 2 for parse errors.
Evaluation failures return their typed status when it is between 1 and 255, otherwise 1.
The Shoal
.B exit CODE
builtin returns CODE without rendering a trailing value.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR shoal-kernel (1),
.BR shoal-history (1),
.BR shoal-secret (1),
.BR shoal-token (1),
.BR shoal-lsp (1),
.BR shoal-mcp (1)
